1. RESEARCH PERMISSION

Each Licensor grants You a worldwide, nonexclusive, royalty-free copyright
licence to copy, install, execute, study and modify its Software for
Permitted Research, and distribute it under clause 3. Permission lasts
for the applicable copyright term, subject to clause 9 and applicable law.
No registration or separate research approval is required.

"Permitted Research" means noncommercial scientific or academic research,
teaching, learning, or verification and reproduction of research results
by educational institutions, nonprofit research organisations or public
research bodies acting in that capacity, or individuals conducting
independent research outside work for a Commercial Entity. It includes
research benchmarks, model training and evaluation, and preparing
publications. Clause 2 takes priority over this permission.

Ordinary salaries, scholarships, tuition, grants and publication fees do
not alone make eligible research commercial. Company employment alone
does not exclude independent personal research, but work within company
duties, on company time, using employer-provided resources or on its behalf
is excluded. You need not publish private modifications or research results.

2. COMPANY USE AND RESEARCH FUNDING

"Commercial Entity" means a for-profit organisation or a person acting in
a trade or business capacity, including a sole trader or a university's
for-profit subsidiary.

Except for clause 5, this Licence grants no permission for any use:
(a) by or on behalf of a Commercial Entity;
(b) in a commercial activity, including commercial activities of academic
    or nonprofit institutions, or to develop, evaluate, improve, operate
    or supply a commercial product or service;
(c) for company-directed or company-commissioned research, or consulting,
    contract research, procurement or investment evaluation for a
    Commercial Entity or as a commercial activity; or
(d) to provide a commercial hosted benchmark, evaluation, training,
    inference or other service incorporating the Software.

These exclusions include internal research, benchmarks, trials, proofs
of concept, model evaluation and employee training within those uses,
even without revenue, sales or redistribution, and even if results are
published. Employees and contractors cannot authorise organisational use
through a personal research licence. There is no free company trial.
Excluded use requires an effective agreement under clause 7 before it begins.

Independent company-funded grants remain eligible where researchers
retain research control and publication freedom. Company-directed or
company-commissioned work, company-specific evaluations, private company
deliverables and exclusive sponsor rights to results are excluded.
Funding acknowledgements, expenditure reports and access to the same
public results available to others do not alone disqualify a grant.
Funding gives the sponsor no permission to use the Software.

3. MODIFICATION AND SHARING

You may distribute the Software, including modifications, for Permitted
Research only if You:
(a) include this complete, unchanged Licence, its project identification
    and contact; retain copyright, attribution, third-party
    notices and accompanying citation instructions; and identify Your
    changes and their dates;
(b) provide complete source for the Software distributed, including
    modifications and necessary build or installation scripts, in the
    preferred form for making changes;
(c) have authority to license every copyrightable modification You
    distribute and offer each under this same TopoBench Research Licence
    1.0, giving recipients permissions directly from its Licensors; and
(d) impose no additional terms, fees or technical restrictions preventing
    exercise of the permissions granted here.

Source must accompany executable or packaged copies or be available at
an accompanying, working download link without additional charge for as
long as You distribute that version. An upstream link omitting changes
is insufficient. Accurate notices for Your contributions may be added.
Other terms require separate authority from the relevant rights holders.

Recipients must independently qualify for their use. These conditions
cover the Software and derivative modifications, not independent programs
merely accompanying or communicating with it. Separately licensed
components retain their terms. Running the Software through another
program does not avoid clause 2.

4. PUBLICATIONS, RESULTS AND MANDATORY CITATION

You may publish and share results of Permitted Research, including through
commercial publishers. Outputs, including papers, measurements, datasets
and model weights, do not acquire this Licence merely because the Software
produced them. No ownership of Your results is claimed; embedded Software
and independent third-party rights retain their applicable terms. Reading,
citing or analysing published results alone requires no commercial
agreement. Publication does not authorise an excluded use of the Software.

As a condition of this Licence's permissions, when publishing or publicly
distributing a paper, thesis, report, presentation or other research output
describing work performed using the Software, You must acknowledge
TopoBench, identify the version or commit used, and cite the principal
publication, "TopoBench: A Framework for Benchmarking Topological Deep
Learning" (https://openreview.net/forum?id=07sTzyEVtY). The README provides
its BibTeX entry. Venue citation styles are acceptable.
This requirement does not oblige You to publish private work.

5. LIMITED INFRASTRUCTURE PERMISSION

Eligible researchers may use ordinary hosting, package distribution,
storage, networking and rented compute for Permitted Research or sharing
under clause 3. Providers may copy, transmit and execute the Software only
as strictly necessary to supply that infrastructure on the researcher's
instructions. Ordinary infrastructure fees do not disqualify the research.
Providers gain no permission for their own research, benchmarking, model
training, product development or other business uses, or to offer a
TopoBench managed application, conduct research or evaluations for
customers, or provide a TopoBench-based service. Those uses require clause 7.

